a tragic story here overnight more  bodies were pulled from the waters off  the California coast where a dive boat  burst into flames and sank the US Coast  Guard says the death toll is at least 25  nine people are still unaccounted for  Jonathan Vigliotti is at the Coast Guard  Station in Oxnard California some 30  miles from where the boat sank Jonathan  what do we know about the victims and  good morning to you hours before that  fire broke out three of the victims  celebrated their birthday one of them a  teenage girl  surrounded by her parents one of the  crew members who escaped said he left  behind his girlfriend most of the  victims were trapped just below deck we  are learning some of their body showing  signs of drowning the boat Concepcion  was anchored just 20 yards off the  Channel Islands near the Ventura  coastline when it caught fire according  to the Coast Guard the first mayday call  came in around 3:30 in the morning the  Coast Guard launched aircraft as well as  boats and located a vessel that was  fully involved in flames the 75 foot  vessel carried dozens of divers on a  holiday excursion when the fire began  many passengers were asleep in their  bunks below deck  the ship's blueprint indicates stairs  leading to the main deck at the front of  the vessel authorities say the company  operating the boat had a good safety  record the crew was actually already  awakened on the bridge and they jumped  off five crew members swam to a nearby  fishing boat owned by Bob and Shirley  Hansen flames and knowing that there are  people on board that cannot get out you  can only imagine a horror that they were  going through  they pulled the crew members to safety  including the ship's captain who told  them a rear escape hatch was engulfed in  fire and the crew could do nothing to  help the passengers one crew member was  inconsolable telling them three  passengers were celebrating birthdays  including a 17 year old there with her  parents he was crying  because he knew they were stolen and  then then the one of the crewmen his  girlfriend was was also on board and she  was down there for family members  arriving at the harbour the reality of  this tragedy still wrong are some  absolute heartbreak the NTSB is headed  here to the scene they will be assisted  by the FBI and officials tell us that  boat is upside down it is unstable under  60 feet of water Tony that is  complicating efforts to recover the rest  of those that were trapped inside all  right Jonathan thank you very much
 

